2. **Attack 2 — F25 & F42 (`4b:3` conflation of passive CSR1/CSR2 retention with `lecsr3stopclear`): BROKEN (DERIVED).**
   `4b:3` (`4:F25`, `4:F42`) states: `The two Am7990 sentences on CSR1/CSR2 across STOP are quoted (:1511-1516 "must be reloaded"; :2853-2857 "normally not affected ... recommended to reload"); neither is implemented (lecsr3stopclear).` Because `src/devices/dev_le.c` has no STOP-clear logic at all (`4:F42`), `d->reg[1]` and `d->reg[2]` passively retain their contents in the `d->reg[]` array when `LE_STOP` is set, while `d->reg[3]` fails to clear. Saying "neither is implemented (`lecsr3stopclear`)" of the CSR1/CSR2 preservation sentences misstates the model's behaviour: `lecsr3stopclear` is the missing clear of CSR3 on STOP (`0:4`), whereas CSR1 and CSR2 remain untouched in `d->reg[1..2]` by default array persistence.

3. **Attack 3 — F25 (`4b:6` past-tense assertion of a post-reset re-fire and follow-up records commit): BROKEN (DERIVED).**
